# Findings the bridge image cannot take a fix for, with what would lift each.
# Read by the image scan in .github/workflows/node-ci.yml. Every other
# fixable HIGH or CRITICAL still fails that job.

# brace-expansion, in npm's own bundled dependencies
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion), pinned at
# 5.0.7 by npm's lockfile. No npm release ships the fix: 12.0.2 is the
# newest and still bundles 5.0.7, though it was published after 5.0.8
# existed. Patching a dependency inside npm's own tree is not something an
# image should do to itself.
#
# Reachability: npm is runtime code here because the bridge launches
# backends through `npx`, and brace-expansion parses glob patterns. What
# reaches it is a package name an operator supplies through `add_backend` —
# a caller who already commands arbitrary execution by design, which is what
# the bridge is for. A denial of service is strictly below what that caller
# already has.
#
# Lift these when an npm release bundles brace-expansion 5.0.9 or later.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
